  "worked_solution": "The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with forced harmonic motion without damping under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ and  external force $F(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{\u2033}=-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m,$ $k$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n6{y}^{\u2033}=-18y+9{e}^{-3t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}+3y=\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-3t}.\n$$",
